message: "If you use UACP in research or products, please cite it as below."
title: "UACP — Universal Agentic Connectivity Protocol"
authors:
  - family-names: Walton
    given-names: Alexander
    alias: Al3xWalton
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-05-05
license: Apache-2.0
url: "https://github.com/Al3xWalton/Universal-Agentic-Connectivity-Protocol"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Al3xWalton/Universal-Agentic-Connectivity-Protocol"
type: standard
keywords:
  - protocol
  - ai-agents
  - connectivity
  - mcp
  - oauth
  - api
  - agents
  - automation
abstract: >-
  UACP is a wire format and runtime contract for describing how an AI
  agent authenticates to and dispatches operations against any HTTPS
  service. UACP is a peer to the Model Context Protocol (MCP): MCP
  standardizes how an agent calls a tool, UACP standardizes how the
  tool, once called, reaches the external service it connects to. The
  two protocols compose. UACP v1.1.0 specifies ten registered
  authentication methods, four schema sources (OpenAPI ingestion,
  curl-paste, LLM inference, browser-captured sessions), four
  pagination patterns, a Connection lifecycle, a security model with
  secret-store registry and audit logging, and a versioning policy
  with a public RFC path to v2.
